pocket-home (0.0.9) trixie; urgency=low

  * Track wifi state from NetworkManager D-Bus signals (GDBus) instead of
    polling nmcli; the launcher wifi icon updates from listener callbacks.
  * Reap launched child processes with a SIGCHLD handler.
  * Get Help opens old.reddit.com; add a Browse Web launcher entry.

 -- Josh Bailey <josh@vandervecken.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 04:44:12 +0000

pocket-home (0.0.8) trixie; urgency=low

  * Port to build on Debian trixie. WifiStatusNM rewritten from libnm-glib
    (removed from trixie) to nmcli for read-only status (polled, drives the wifi
    icon) + nmtui for all configuration; drops the libnm-glib build/runtime deps.
  * debian/rules: build NATIVELY (build.sh runs us in an armhf container) instead
    of forcing CXX=arm-linux-gnueabihf-g++; skip the non-existent auto install/
    test targets (debian/install handles file placement).
  * debian/control: debhelper compat 13, drop libnm-glib-dev/network-manager-dev/
    libnm-glib4, add libasound2-dev + libxext-dev; depend on network-manager +
    x-terminal-emulator (for nmtui).
  * Settings page: the wifi button (showing the connected SSID) now launches a
    terminal running nmtui instead of opening the removed in-app network list. The
    command is configurable via config.json "wifiCommand" (default
    "lxterminal -e nmtui"). The wifi row keeps only the on/off toggle + SSID label;
    the home-screen wifi corner icon stays a display-only signal indicator.
  * Pressing the wifi button shows the same launch spinner the home-screen apps
    use. The spinner moved from LauncherComponent up to MainContentComponent (the
    top-level overlay layer) so it renders over any page, not just the app menu.

 -- Ben Young <computermouth@proton.me>  Thu, 18 Jun 2026 05:00:00 -0500

